  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The REST API does not have the equivalent of API-M getDatastreams.  Instead it is necessary to list datastreams using the /objects/pid/datastreams endpoint and then iterate each of the datastreams.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Add getDatastreams to the REST API.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "For discussion:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "should this be a different endpoint to the /objects/pid/datastereams endpoint?",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "or should we add a URL parameter on the same endpoint?",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "need to consider any AuthZ implications (as listDatastreams is API-A and getDatastreams is API-M)",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    }
   ],
